  "summary": "Kootenai County commissioners declined to renew the sheriff's office's $24,000 annual automatic license plate reader contract, ending the program at the end of 2025. Commissioners cited budget priorities and constituent opposition, while the sheriff's office defended the technology's crime-fighting benefits.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Kootenai County Sheriff's Office will lose automatic license plate reader technology after commissioners decided not to renew the $24,000 annual contract.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "We do have higher priorities, like cost of living adjustments and wages, wage increases for the county and the sheriff's department",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "We've had a town hall and I get calls and emails from constituents quite often. They just don't like the idea of the mobile license plate reader",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
